[
  // ── THE MASTERY LADDER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // What repeating one action a hundred times actually buys. One shared ladder rather than a
  // mastery block on each of the 659 actions — that would be 659 places for a balance pass to
  // miss one.
  //
  // Mastery level is mastery points, one per completed attempt, to a ceiling of 99
  // (MasteryLeveling — deliberately linear, see its doc comment). So "per_level" reads as
  // "per completed attempt" today, and every number below is exactly what the four hardcoded
  // constants in ProfessionTuning used to be. THIS FILE CHANGED NOTHING ABOUT HOW AN ACTION
  // FEELS — it moved the numbers somewhere a balance pass can reach them.
  //
  // ── THE TWO NEW RUNGS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Preservation and doubling are the Melvor layers GDD §4.1 has carried as "Planned" since the
  // first commit. Both have an unlock_level, which is the point: they are things that START
  // HAPPENING, not another percentage creeping up from zero. Doubling costs more than
  // preservation because doubling makes materials and preservation only saves them.
  //
  // ── WHY THE CAPS ARE NOT ROUND ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Each "max" is exactly what its rate reaches at mastery 99, because the validator refuses a
  // cap the ceiling cannot deliver — a promise the ladder can never keep is worse than a smaller
  // honest one. So interval buys 0.495, not "half".
  //
  // ONE NUMBER GENUINELY MOVED: opportunity risk. Its old cap of 0.5 needed 250 completions of a
  // single action, which the old uncapped point counter could reach and a 99-level track cannot.
  // Capped at what 99 levels actually buy (0.198) rather than raising the rate, because raising
  // it would be a mid-track buff — a balance decision, and balance is parked.
  //
  // ── STILL UNBALANCED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Every number here is the placeholder it was before it moved. Nobody has played to mastery.

  {
    "id": "mastery.interval",
    "kind": "IntervalReduction",
    "unlock_level": 1,
    "per_level": 0.005,
    "max": 0.495,
    "description": "The work goes quicker."
  },
  {
    "id": "mastery.bonus_output",
    "kind": "BonusOutputChance",
    "unlock_level": 1,
    "per_level": 0.0025,
    "max": 0.2475,
    "description": "You turn up the uncommon finds more often."
  },
  {
    "id": "mastery.preservation",
    "kind": "InputPreservation",
    "unlock_level": 20,
    "per_level": 0.004,
    "max": 0.3,
    "description": "Sometimes the materials survive the work."
  },
  {
    "id": "mastery.doubling",
    "kind": "OutputDoubling",
    "unlock_level": 40,
    "per_level": 0.003,
    "max": 0.25,
    "description": "Sometimes the work yields twice."
  },
  {
    "id": "mastery.opportunity",
    "kind": "OpportunityChance",
    "unlock_level": 1,
    "per_level": 0.001,
    "max": 0.099,
    "description": "You notice what a stranger to this work would walk past."
  },
  {
    "id": "mastery.opportunity_risk",
    "kind": "OpportunityRisk",
    "unlock_level": 1,
    "per_level": 0.002,
    "max": 0.198,
    "description": "You know which chances are worth taking."
  }
]
